# Halcyon's leaders, the hub (docs/DIALOGUE.md, "Hubs: work comes out of talk"): 0 the job, 1 the
# built news, 2 what they make of you, each carried by a topic. Voice: precise, a bit cold,
# sometimes guilty. Humour only by accident. Halcyon talks in numbers.

conv halcyon.leader.work_samples
for stronghold:halcyon, seat:halcyon/field_lead
when need:samples
topic "Ask what the count is short of."
prio ask
voice halcyon

node start
  jump route:out -> other_route
  jump epilogue -> after
  say? stronghold :: "Tissue. Fresh, from the infected, under six hours old. We have three samples. We need eleven."
  say? trait:idealist :: "Samples. I know what that word sounds like. It's the only word that gets us to the cure."
  say "Samples. The work stops without them. The work cannot stop."
  say "We're at {cure_percent} percent. Every point costs something that used to walk."
  > @what "What sort of samples?" -> what
  > @who "Whose samples?" -> whose
  > @worth "What do I get?" -> worth
  > @lab "Your chain of custody is a mess." -> custody   if bg:labtech,doctor,nurse
  > @help "Is there work in it for me?" -> offer
  > @no "Not today." -> hub

node what
  say "Blood, tissue, a sample of the fluid behind the eye. We provide the kit. You provide the nerve."
  say "Sealed, labelled, cold. Under six hours, or it's a souvenir."
  > @help2 "I can do cold." -> offer
  > @back1 "Something else." -> hub

node whose
  say "The dead ones. The infected. Nobody living, if that's your question. That's always the first question."
  say? major:proof :: "The second question is the one the Haven keeps asking about our volunteers. Ask it somewhere else."
  say "It's a fair question. I'd ask it."
  > @help3 "Then I'll bring them." -> offer
  > @back2 "Something else." -> hub

node worth
  say? trait:greedy :: "Favor. A place in the queue for the first doses. The queue is the only thing in the Zone that's worth more every day."
  say "Favor, and our gratitude, which we record. In triplicate."
  > @help4 "Triplicate it is." -> offer
  > @back3 "Something else." -> hub

node custody
  say "It is. Two of my four field staff can't spell 'contaminated'. You can, apparently."
  say "Bring them sealed and dated and I'll stop apologising to the director."
  > @help5 "Then let me bring them in properly." -> offer
  > @back4 "Something else." -> hub

node offer
  say "There's tasking. It's described exactly. Please read the description exactly."
  > @take "Show me." -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @later "Let me think about it." -> hub

node other_route
  say "You've committed to another route for the cure. It's in your file. The file doesn't stop us using you."
  > @take2 "Is there work anyway?" -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @back5 "Something else." -> hub

node after
  say? cure_held:halcyon :: "We hold the cure. The work now is making enough of it, and deciding who's first. The second part isn't science."
  say "The cure exists. The work isn't finished. It's never finished. It's just less urgent."
  > @take3 "Then I'll still work." -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @back6 "Something else." -> hub

conv halcyon.leader.work
for stronghold:halcyon, seat:halcyon/field_lead
when !need:samples
topic "Ask what the lab needs."
prio ask
voice halcyon

node start
  jump route:out -> other_route
  jump epilogue -> after
  say? need:security :: "Guards. The lab has two doors and four guards. One of the doors doesn't lock. I've stopped writing that down."
  say? need:supplies :: "Reagents, filters, generator fuel. If the power drops for forty minutes, two weeks of cultures die."
  say? need:people :: "Hands. Clean ones. The volunteers are not staff, whatever the rota says."
  say "Time. We need time, and the only way to buy it is people bringing us things."
  say? cure>=90 :: "We are past ninety. Everyone wants to be in the room when it finishes. Nobody wants to be in the room if it doesn't."
  say? finale:open :: "And four factions want the cure to belong to them. We'd like it to work first."
  say "We're at {cure_percent} percent. The last ten are the slowest. They always are."
  > @why "Why is it so slow?" -> slow
  > @risk "What happens if the power goes?" -> power
  > @press "What aren't the numbers saying?" -> told | partial | partial   check persuade halcyon 2 harder:paranoid bg:labtech,doctor
  > @help "Give me something to do." -> offer
  > @no "Not today." -> hub

node slow
  say "Because every step is a test, and every test is a person or a part of one. We go as fast as the dead allow."
  > @help2 "Then let me speed it up." -> offer
  > @back1 "Something else." -> hub

node power
  say "We lose two weeks. Possibly three. We'd survive. Some of the cultures would not. Neither, possibly, would I."
  > @help3 "Then let me keep it running." -> offer
  > @back2 "Something else." -> hub

node told
  say "The trial doses. One in three takes. That's an improvement. The other two are also a number."
  say "I'd like you to remember both."
  do learn:halcyon.one_in_three:6h
  > @help4 "I'll remember. What can I do?" -> offer
  > @back3 "Something else." -> hub

node partial
  say "The numbers are saying everything. You're not listening to all of them. Neither is anyone."
  > @help5 "Then give me work instead." -> offer
  > @back4 "Something else." -> hub

node offer
  say? trait:ruthless :: "There's work. The form was short."
  say "There's tasking. It's described exactly. Please read the description exactly."
  > @take "Show me." -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @later "Let me think about it." -> hub

node other_route
  say "You've committed to another route for the cure. It's in your file. The file doesn't stop us using you."
  > @take2 "Is there work anyway?" -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @back5 "Something else." -> hub

node after
  say "The cure exists. The rest is logistics, and grief, and paperwork about both."
  > @take3 "Then give me some paperwork." -> hub   do call:slot:0
  > @back6 "Something else." -> hub

conv halcyon.leader.news
for stronghold:halcyon, seat:halcyon/field_lead
topic "Ask what the radio logs say."
prio world
voice halcyon

bind dead = news:leader_dead
bind horde = news:horde
bind over = news:overrun
bind took = news:taken
bind who = news:taken_by

node start
  jump news:leader_dead -> dead
  jump news:overrun -> overrun
  jump news:horde -> horde
  jump news:taken -> taken
  say? epilogue :: "The logs say processing at the road checkpoints. Ninety-one percent of messages since are people asking what processing means."
  say? edge :: "The logs say the drones flew their usual pattern. Fourteen passes a day. We counted. Counting is calming."
  say? outbreak:overrun :: "The logs say the infected are adapting. Faster than we are. That's a measurement, not an opinion."
  say "The logs say what they always say. Forty messages a day, six worth keeping."
  > @mine "What does your file say about me?" -> me
  > @more "Anything else in the logs?" -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @back0 "Something else." -> hub

node dead
  say "{bind:dead} is dead. I've added the name to a list. We keep a lot of lists."
  say? trait:idealist :: "It shouldn't feel like a statistic. It does. I'm sorry for that, not that it matters."
  > @more1 "What else is in the logs?" -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @back1 "Something else." -> hub

node overrun
  say "{bind:over} has passed eighty on our infection index. That's what we call overrun when we're being polite."
  say "If you're going there, take a sample kit. If you're not going there, good."
  > @more2 "What else is in the logs?" -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @back2 "Something else." -> hub

node horde
  say "A group of them moved near {bind:horde}. Somewhere between forty and sixty, by the noise. They follow sound."
  say "Somebody ran a generator. Generators are the dinner bell of the modern age."
  > @more3 "What else is in the logs?" -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @back3 "Something else." -> hub

node taken
  say "{bind:who} holds {bind:took} now. It changes nothing for the lab. It changes everything for the people there."
  > @more4 "What else is in the logs?" -> hub   do call:slot:1
  > @back4 "Something else." -> hub

node me
  jump kit:other -> me_colours
  say? best:halcyon :: "That you {best}. Noted with a date. Dates are how we say thank you."
  say? symptoms :: "That you're symptomatic. That's in the file in red. Red means come and see us before the end."
  say "A file with your name on it and two lines of notes. Two is more than most."
  > @back5 "Something else." -> hub

node me_colours
  say "That you came in another faction's clothes. Recorded as an observation, not a judgment."
  > @back6 "Something else." -> hub

conv halcyon.leader.me
for stronghold:halcyon, seat:halcyon/field_lead
topic "Ask how they'd file you."
prio reaction
voice halcyon

node start
  jump kit:other -> colours
  jump bite_shown -> bitten
  jump tier:halcyon>=trusted -> trusted
  jump tier:halcyon>=known -> known
  say? fresh :: "New. One page. Most of it blank. Blank is not a bad result."
  say "Subject: unaffiliated. Useful: not yet measured. That's not an insult. It's a column."
  > @more "And what's in the column now?" -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @fair "Fair." -> hub

node colours
  say "You're wearing someone else's colours in a sterile area. Two problems. I've ranked them."
  > @more1 "And otherwise?" -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @back1 "Something else." -> hub

node bitten
  say "Bite visible. Under twelve hours, by the colour. You know where the lab is. I'd prefer you came in walking."
  say? declared :: "You told a house. That's in your favour, in the file and otherwise."
  > @more2 "Am I still welcome here?" -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @back2 "Something else." -> hub

node trusted
  say? title:halcyon :: "Staff call you {title:halcyon}. They don't name anyone. Two of them argued about it for a day."
  say "Reliable. That's the highest word we use. It sounds small. In here it's a medal."
  > @more3 "The full file?" -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @back3 "Something else." -> hub

node known
  say? jobs:halcyon>=3 :: "Three tasks, completed to specification. Statistically, you're a pattern."
  say "Known to the lab. The guards will use your name. They'll still check your hands."
  > @more4 "And where do I stand?" -> hub   do call:slot:2
  > @back4 "Something else." -> hub
